A when that tests an optional field's presence and reads it. Reading it
already restricts the lacuna to the instances that have it, and to test
presence alone the field is named bare.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name:   string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name:  string
	count: int
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		count: _coalesce(v0_0.count, 0)
	}
	lacunas: {
		count: [{
			type:    PrecisionLoss
			message: "counts above 1000 are rounded downstream"
			when:    v0_0.count != _|_ && v0_0.count > 1000
		}]
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	name:  string
	count: int
}
-- out/error --
error[E0423]: this condition tests the presence of v0_0.count, which it also reads
  --> history/1.0.thema:15:13
   |
15 |             when:    v0_0.count != _|_ && v0_0.count > 1000
   |                      ^^^^
   |
   = note: a condition reading an optional field concerns only the instances that have it, so testing its presence says nothing more
   = help: drop the presence test; to test presence alone, write when: v0_0.count
